{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Ozen","id":"321508500138360843","is_bot":0,"username":"ozenannwn"},"author_id":"321508500138360843","channel_id":"739055141759615027","content":"Selene stretches with a little shake to shed the sleep as if it were snow. They make way over to the waters edge and cup some to drink a donkey meanders over from where they slept to join them at the water.","created_at":"2020-08-04T15:37:48.144000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"740232027256651806","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Sketchy Bee 🐝","id":"297577343554158603","is_bot":0,"username":"sketchybee"},"author_id":"297577343554158603","channel_id":"739055141759615027","content":"Leaf wakes up with a loud, lazy yawn as she stretches awake. She sits up and groggily watches the fish in the pond for a while, before noticing something across the way... Two statues. Amara and Navar. She quietly walks over to them and sits between them, looking out over the water, just thinking. After a long while she finally speaks out loud, \"Amara, I'm sorry if what I did put you in danger. You should know I haven't held Zone of Truth or Command with me since. I don't plan to. It made me feel icky. I want the magic Mello gives me to bring happiness like she does, not fear. And I'll be sure to dance eventually. I want that to be able to make me happy too. I know you cared a lot for Castor, so I'll do my best to keep an ear out for him... Even if he still calls me young.\" She chuckles at the last part.","created_at":"2020-08-04T19:04:59.223000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"740284166981025822","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Sketchy Bee 🐝","id":"297577343554158603","is_bot":0,"username":"sketchybee"},"author_id":"297577343554158603","channel_id":"739055141759615027","content":"Leaf sits for a moment, as if politely waiting for a response, then turning to Navar she says, \"Navar, I- I know you wouldn't want me to be sad. It's just... There were so many things I was looking forward to doing here, but it doesn't feel the same without you. There was so much I wanted ask and learn. We we're supposed to find our gods together... it's funny... I'd been praying in Elvish this whole time because I thought I had to be, I don't know, fancy? Civilized? For Melora. Like I wasn't good enough. But I finally met her and,\" Leaf laughs, \"I don't think she cares about any of that!\" she smiles. \"I hope wherever you are that you're with Chauntea. And if not, maybe we'll be able to find her too. I'm no knight, but they seem to know a lot. Maybe Mello knows too! But you never gave up hope, so I won't either.\"","created_at":"2020-08-04T19:05:26.210000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"740284280172970110","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Sketchy Bee 🐝","id":"297577343554158603","is_bot":0,"username":"sketchybee"},"author_id":"297577343554158603","channel_id":"739055141759615027","content":"She smiles and sits in the late morning sun, letting a weight be lifted off her chest. Maybe it's just her imagination, but she swears she can hear a hummingbird wiz by her ear. She doesn't turn to look, but closes her eyes to enjoy the sound. \"Ebuc... I still don't know what was going on in that head of yours. I suppose I never really will, and maybe it's better that way. You still believed you were on the right path, so at least maybe you were at peace. You also believed in me, which sometimes I feel silly about given how little I believe in myself. I'm not sure how the others will remember you, but I'll always remember the good parts. Like the time you came to apologise to all of us on the rooftops even though you were afraid of heights. And talking Goblin together on the sub. I'm glad I had the chance to tell you how much that meant to me.\" She smiles, opening her eyes again. She feels happy, this time her own happiness. She stands and turns to the direction she imagines the shore is. With an air of finality she shouts, \"And Tir Na Nog, I'm happy to see you gone! I hope that kraken dragged all those dark secrets and scary cult rituals right to the bottom of the sea where they belong!!\" She stomps her foot to prove how serious she is, but laughs anyway. She walks away from the oasis finally joyfull for the first time since coming to Roanoke. She decides it's time she found a tree to call home, where she can have her new family over and watch the stars.\n( <@361351593292988425> <@339235123759153162> <@456226577798135808> )","created_at":"2020-08-04T19:05:36.210000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"740284322115879093","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
